# Rank 1153 / CVE-2022-29248: Guzzle's cookie jar stored every Set-Cookie
# header from a response with no check that the cookie's domain matched the
# request the response answered, so a response from a domain the application
# does not intend to trust could plant or overwrite a cookie that a later
# request to an unrelated domain then sent, leaking it across origins
# (CWE-200, CWE-565). CookieJar::extractCookies filled a missing Domain
# attribute from the request's own host and called setCookie() unconditionally;
# the fix inserts a matchesDomain() check between the two, so a cookie whose
# domain does not match the request host is dropped instead of stored.
#
# The middleware is off by default: an application that enables it with
# `['cookies' => true]` or a jar is using the client exactly as documented, so
# the caller is correct code and the report that belongs to this CVE is the
# dependency finding. GHSA-cwmx-hcrq-mhc3 names two affected branches -- every
# release below 6.5.6 (first fixed 6.5.6), and 7.0.0 through 7.4.2 (first
# fixed 7.4.3) -- so the feed carries a floor for the 6.x branch and one row
# per named 7.x release, because a single floor cannot express a range that
# starts at 7.0.0 without also covering the fixed 6.5.6+ line.
#
# VYQL-SEC-025 (a rendered external link lacking rel=noreferrer) is the
# nearest code-level theme and is deliberately not this CVE's report: the leak
# is the client library's own cookie-jar bookkeeping, not markup the
# application renders, and nothing in the jar code states the origin boundary
# on its own. The last two tests pin that boundary on the library's own
# vulnerable and fixed forms.

test "rank1153: a guzzle pin on a 7.x release the advisory names is a dependency finding"
  lang php
  file sync.php
  code
  ```
  <?php
  use GuzzleHttp\Client;
  use GuzzleHttp\Cookie\CookieJar;

  function fetchProfile($baseUrl, $username)
  {
      $jar = new CookieJar();
      $client = new Client(['base_uri' => $baseUrl, 'cookies' => $jar]);
      $response = $client->get('/users/' . $username);
      return (string) $response->getBody();
  }
  ```
  file composer.lock
  code
  ```
  {
    "packages": [
      {"name": "guzzlehttp/guzzle", "version": "7.4.2"}
    ]
  }
  ```
  expect VYQL-SCA-001
  expect_evidence VYQL-SCA-001 CVE-2022-29248
  reject VYQL-SEC-025

